.\" ROADMAP-AGENT manual page
.TH ROADMAP-AGENT 1 "2026-04-12" "ROADMAP-AGENT" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
roadmap-agent \- terminal-first roadmap workflow with optional MemPalace and MCP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B roadmap-agent
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.br
.B rma
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ROADMAP-AGENT manages product context and roadmap state in plain Markdown under
\fB.rma/\fR, drives LLM-backed \fBplan\fR and \fBanalyze\fR, optional MemPalace
retrieval (\fBmempalace wake-up\fR for \fBplan\fR when \fB.rma/mempalace\fR exists),
and exposes an optional Model Context Protocol server (\fBrma_mcp\fR) for IDE hosts.
.PP
Default behavior with no command opens the interactive hub (\fBfzf\fR when available).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create \fB.rma/\fR templates and roadmap paths. Options: \fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR;
\fB\-\-embed\fR / \fB\-\-no\-embed\fR for toolkit copy into the managed project.
.TP
.B status
Show project, branch, and roadmap/task summary.
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnostics: PATH, Python venv, LLM providers, MemPalace imports, persistence.
Use \fB\-\-json\fR for machine-readable output (web UI and scripts).
.TP
.B plan
Generate \fB.rma/roadmaps/plan.md\fR via configured LLM. Optional interactive
prompts for open questions (\fB.rma/open\-questions.md\fR, \fBOpen:\fR lines in context
files). \fB\-\-no\-interactive\fR skips prompts. Optional MemPalace \fBwake\-up\fR text
when \fB.rma/mempalace\fR exists.
.TP
.B analyze
Scan the tree and sync \fBtasks.md\fR / \fBrun.md\fR under \fB.rma/roadmaps/\fR.
.TP
.B analyze\-init
LLM/heuristic proposals for the four context files. Flags: \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR,
\fB\-\-yes\fR, \fB\-\-require\-ollama\fR.
.TP
.B execute\-one
Select one unchecked task from \fBplan.md\fR and run the guarded execution path.
.TP
.B agent / run\-agent
Autonomous agent loop (\fBrma_agent\fR by default; \fBRMA_AGENT_LEGACY=1\fR for bash loop).
Options: \fB\-\-max\-steps\fR, \fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-confirm\-execute\-one\fR, \fB\-\-require\-ollama\fR.
.TP
.B tools
Print JSON manifest of CLI tools for external agents.
.TP
.B unlock
Clear stale roadmap lock.
.TP
.B persistence / persistance
Install global launchers and runtime (admin/root on Unix; Administrator on Windows).
.TP
.B persistence\-check
Report install status and offer upgrade.
.TP
.B setup\-venv
Create or refresh \fB.rma/venv\fR and install MemPalace/ChromaDB (OS setup script).
.TP
.B pick\-env
Choose a project \fB.env*\fR file and copy to \fB.env\fR.
.TP
.B web\-api / web\-backend
Start FastAPI companion UI backend (default port 8765; see \fBRMA_WEB_*\fR).
.TP
.B web\-frontend
Start Vite dev server for the companion SPA (default 5173).
.TP
.B mcp\-start
Start MCP server (\fBrma_mcp\fR): \fBstreamable\-http\fR, \fBsse\fR, or \fBstdio\fR
(\fBRMA_MCP_*\fR). See \fBdocs/MCP\-SERVER.md\fR.
.TP
.B release
Maintainer: tag, Docker build, GitHub release from \fBVERSION\fR and \fBCHANGELOG\fR
(\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR, \fB\-\-skip\-*\fR, \fB\-y\fR).
.TP
.B man
Show this manual text when \fBnroff\fR is unavailable.
.TP
.B help \fR/ \fB\-h \fR/ \fB\-\-help
Detailed help (same topics as environment variables in \fB.env.example\fR).
.TP
.B menu
Interactive hub (Roadmap, MemPalace, Environment, Web/MCP, Maintainer).
.SH MEMPALACE
\fBmempalace mine\fR indexes project files into a local palace; menu entries may use
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR. \fBplan\fR does not call a MemPalace \fBplan\fR subcommand; it uses
your LLM plus optional \fBwake\-up\fR retrieval. Environment: \fBRMA_REQUIRE_MEMPALACE\fR,
\fBRMA_MEMPALACE_BIN\fR, \fBRMA_MEMPALACE_MINE_DIR\fR. Local palace data under
\fB.rma/mempalace\fR should not be committed to version control.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .rma/description.md
Product/function context.
.TP
.B .rma/ui.md
UI/UX or CLI behavior expectations.
.TP
.B .rma/stack.md
Stack and versions.
.TP
.B .rma/other.md
Operational constraints and decisions.
.TP
.B .rma/roadmaps/plan.md
Generated dry\-run plan.
.TP
.B .rma/roadmaps/tasks.md \fR/ \fBrun.md
Synced task and run state.
.TP
.B .rma/mempalace/
Local MemPalace data (gitignored).
.TP
.B .rma/mcp/
MCP runtime logs and \fBruntime.json\fR when using HTTP transport.
